Extension Readiness

Overview

The refactored UNO project was redesigned with modularity and maintainability in mind.

The system is now separated into specialized utility classes, making the application easier to extend and improve in future versions.


Current Modular Structure

The project separates responsibilities across multiple classes:

Main → application coordination
CardRules → card validation and rule processing
BotStrategy → automated bot logic
ConsolePrompter → user input handling
ScoreCalculator → score computation

This structure reduces coupling between components and improves code organization.

Future Extension Possibilities

The current architecture allows several future improvements to be implemented with minimal modifications.

Possible extensions include:

Graphical User Interface (GUI)

The console interaction layer is isolated inside ConsolePrompter, making it easier to replace with a GUI implementation.

Multiplayer Support

Additional player management systems can be added without changing card rule logic.

Advanced Bot AI

The BotStrategy class can be expanded with more sophisticated decision-making algorithms.

Additional UNO Rules

Custom rules and house rules can be implemented inside CardRules while preserving the rest of the system.

Save/Load Features

Game state serialization can be added without major restructuring.

Maintainability Benefits

The refactoring improves maintainability by:

reducing duplicated logic
isolating responsibilities
improving readability
simplifying debugging and testing

Each class now has a clearly defined purpose, making future development safer and more efficient.

Conclusion

The refactored project is well-prepared for future extensions due to its modular structure and separation of concerns.
The new architecture supports scalability, easier maintenance, and cleaner integration of future features.
